Ground_Collision: contiguous rotation matrices (scattered-locals class)

Ground_Collision (car-landing dynamics) builds three 3x3 short matrices on the
stack and multiplies them into the car's rotation matrix @car+0x50 via
MulMatrix2 chains; Ghidra split each into 4-6 scalars, gcc scatters them ->
the landing orientation came out scrambled. Watchpoint-proven writer of the
L2 cf134 native/wasm divergence (first 6 diff bytes, car6 matrix +0x5c, via
Car_Landed_On_Corner -> Ground_Collision -> MulMatrix2 with a stack source
matrix). Same class as patches 530/535/540.

